# Klipper, a printer's firmware run from a small computer beside it.
# Written from Klipper's public documentation (klipper3d.org, "G-Codes"),
# no firmware source.
#
# Klipper takes the common G-code: G28 homes, M140/M190 set the bed and
# wait, M104/M109 the hotend, M82 measures E from the start, G92 E0 sets
# E, M107 stops the fan, M84 lets the motors go. Many printers have their
# own start and end macros (PRINT_START ...): put yours in a copy of the
# profile's start and end in place of these. A job is a file, uploaded
# over the network to the computer that runs Klipper.
family = printer
dialect = klipper
send = file network
features = heated-bed homing
extruders = 1
start = G21 ; mm
start += G90 ; absolute moves
start += M82 ; absolute extrusion
start += M140 S{bed}
start += M104 S{hotend}
start += G28 ; home
start += M190 S{bed}
start += M109 S{hotend}
start += G92 E0
end = M104 S0
end += M140 S0
end += M107
end += G91
end += G1 Z5 F600 ; lift clear of the part
end += G90
end += M84
